# ~/.zprofile — deliberately (almost) empty. Do NOT add PATH lines here.
#
# This file is managed by chezmoi purely so it cannot silently regrow. It runs
# on every LOGIN shell, after .zshenv and before .zshrc, and installers love to
# append unguarded `export PATH="$PATH:..."` lines to it. The JetBrains Toolbox
# installer did exactly that, which meant every login shell got a second copy of
# that entry appended to an already-correct PATH. (That entry now lives in
# .zshenv, behind a strip-then-append guard that cannot duplicate.)
#
# PATH belongs in exactly two places:
#   ~/.zshenv  — sets it for ALL shells (scripts, cron, GUI apps, agent shells)
#   ~/.zshrc   — RE-ASSERTS priority, because macOS /etc/zprofile runs
#                `path_helper` in between these two files, which rebuilds PATH
#                with /usr/bin & friends hoisted to the front.
#
# If an installer appends a PATH line here, move it to ~/.zshenv instead.
